{"name":"Titanium Man","hex":"#bcb9c0","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"titanium","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A chemical element (symbol Ti), atomic number 22; it is a strong, corrosion-resistant transition metal, used to make light alloys for aircraft etc.","An atom of this element."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/titanium"},{"term":"man","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Mandingo."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An adult male human.","All human males collectively: mankind."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/man"}],"entries":[{"title":"Titanium Man","blocks":[{"text":"The Titanium Man is the name of two supervillains appearing in American comic books published by Marvel Comics. The original Titanium Man, Boris Bullski, first appeared in Tales of Suspense #69 and was created by Stan Lee and Don Heck."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/af/Titaniummanwarmachine.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Titanium_Man"},{"title":"Titanium","blocks":[{"text":"Titanium is a chemical element; it has symbol Ti and atomic number 22. Found in nature only as an oxide, it can be reduced to produce a lustrous transition metal with a silver color, low density, and high strength that is resistant to corrosion in sea water, aqua regia, and chlorine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Titan-crystal_bar.JPG/330px-Titan-crystal_bar.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Titanium"},{"title":"Man","blocks":[{"text":"A man is an adult male human. Before adulthood, a male child or adolescent is referred to as a boy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Outdoors-man-portrait_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Outdoors-man-portrait_%28croppe